[[_searching]]
=== Searching
tag::concept[]

As the SketchSpark project grows to hundreds of files and thousands of commits, Nora and her team need a way to find specific information quickly. Git provides several built-in tools for searching through your history and your files.

==== Git Grep
tag::procedure[]

(((git commands, grep)))
Suppose Nora needs to find every file that references the "early-adopter" persona. Instead of using her computer's built-in search (which might be slow or include deleted files), she uses `git grep`.

[source,bash]
----
$ git grep "early-adopter"
research/personas/early-adopter.md:## Early Adopter Profile
research/interview-notes/2026-03-12.md:Mentioned the "early-adopter" goals...
----

`git grep` is incredibly fast because it only searches the files in your Git repository. It can also search older versions of your project. If Nora wants to see where that term was used in an old tag:

[source,bash]
----
$ git grep "early-adopter" v0.1-concept
----

==== Tracing the Evolution of a Line
tag::procedure[]

One of the most powerful tools for a designer is the **Line Log**. Suppose Sam wants to see how a specific design token—like the `primary-blue` color—has changed over time.

He can tell Git to show him every commit that touched a specific range of lines in a file. If the color token is on line 5 of `design-tokens.json`:

[source,bash]
----
$ git log -L 5,5:design-tokens.json
----

Git will show Sam a "micro-history" of just that one line. He can see every time the color was tweaked, who changed it, and why. This is a game-changer for auditing design systems and understanding how a project's visual language has evolved.

==== Searching Commit Messages
tag::procedure[]

Nora can also search through her team's "ledger of decisions" using the `--grep` flag with `git log`. To see all commits related to "Contrast":

[source,bash]
----
$ git log --grep="Contrast"
----

By using these search tools, Nora and Sam can treat their repository as a **living archive**, making it easy to find any decision or asset in seconds.
